From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tristin Baker <tristinbaker@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:19:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add OE_GAMEPAD_MENU_NAVIGATION: navigate menus with the d-pad
 and the mouse cursor

In menus the dialog d-pad bindings move the mouse cursor to the nearest thing to click in that direction: buttons,
inventory and chest cells, equipped items on the paper doll (HitMap::visiblePoints). The dialog select binding
clicks there and Square right-clicks, but only over something to click, so the menus' own gamepad hotkeys keep
working elsewhere. Menus are the windows open above the game's interface, or all of them in the main menu.

Most menus have no keyboard navigation, and the game menu's and spellbook's show no selection or can't move
freely, so with a gamepad there was no way through the inventory or the game menu without a mouse. Windows whose
own keyboard navigation works (party creation, NPC and house dialogues) keep it: party creation's columns are big
buttons, and taking over the d-pad and the select button there left no way to change stats or press OK.

The touchpad mouse no longer hides its cursor in menus, it shows where the navigation is.
